      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum of **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release metformin, and the extended-release maximum is 2000 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum), or\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do intend 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a reason, and I'll add it to the order note so pharmacy can review it."
      }
     ],
